d the difference between first and second was greater than that between 2nd and 12th."] "\n\n" [:p {} "A three way contest to decide silver and bronze developed between The Netherlands, Spain and USA. The performance of " [:a {:href "/athletes/11324"} "Beatriz Ferrer-Salat"] ", well supported by " [:a {:href "/athletes/90678"} "Juan Antonio Jiménez"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/12774"} "Rafael Soto"] ", provided second placed Spain with a first ever dressage medal and despite the presence of reigning Olympic champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/11490"} "Anky van Grunsven"] ", the US team edged the Netherlands to the bronze medal. Spain’s medal broke the run of three Olympic Games where Germany, the Netherlands and the USA had finished in the exact same order at the top of the leaderboard."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "Horse"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Judge E Scores"] [:th {} "Judge H Scores"] [:th {} "Judge C Scores"] [:th {} "Judge M Scores"] [:th {} "Judge B Scores"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Germany"] [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "74.653"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "228"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/90701"} "Ulla Salzgeber"] " "] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/2177"} "Rusty 47"]]] [:td {}] [:td {} "78.208"] [:td {} "77.708"] [:td {} "77.917"] [:td {} "81.667"] [:td {} "76.042"] [:td {} "77.708"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "229"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12707"} "Martin Schaudt"] " 